Z||000000||shiloh187||03-23-2001||02:12 AM||||Hey guys, I am sorry to annoy you with this as I know it gets asked alot but i am asking again because i am lost.<P>I have an 87 Iron Duke and I would like to do a stereo install in it.  Now, I am not very mechanically inclined so please if you want to help me, have patience  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I purchased two Rockford Fosgate RFX1408 (8 Inch Subs) and would like to have them mounted behind the seats.  I really like FieroSounds setup, but i am not certain how hard that would be to do.  I am sure I can build the custom box if i had the dimensions on it, and I have someone who can cut the firewall, but I am looking for instructions from someone so that I know exactly what I am doing, and what i need to get.<P>If this solution is indeed very difficult, what would you all recommend?  I want them to be as stealth as possible.<P>Thank You all in advance..<P>shiloh||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||03-23-2001||09:14 AM||||You are talking about actualy cutting away part of your firewall, fiberglassing the shape to be airtight, and then construscting an enclosure over that with wood that will be airtight, and you ask if it will be difficult?<BR>I have a lot of respect for installs like that, because they rate very high on the degree of difficulty scale. It is extremely stealth if done right, I'd be terrified of screwing something up and ruining the value of my car.<P>Just an idea. Since bass in non-directional, there is really no benefit to a symmetrical mounting. A removable enclosure mounted in the passenger footwell could potentially hold 2 8" subs and take up very little room. Here's the one I made for my car using a 10" sub. There is a lot of legroom left.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=34099626&Sequence=5&res=high">   <BR>Here's a thread to tell you how to make you own, or I could build you one for you for $150 shipped. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005771.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005771.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 03-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||fyerstarter||03-23-2001||09:46 PM||||STIMPY!  Dude, you rule  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I've been contemplating building a box there for while now but I never thought of glassing the back. I was always gonna use wood which would majorly restrict my air space. Kicking myself now for not thinking of that :P Your tha man.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||03-23-2001||09:54 PM||||yes, stimpy is da man.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>he gave me the idea of putting a sub in the footwell. i did mine a little different though. pretty good for my first try too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">with mine, you can't see the sub. but you can still tell something is down there. not as clean of an install as stimp's, but it sounds great!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000004||ferrari_momo||03-23-2001||10:05 PM||||ummm, what about stuffing the speakers in the trunk and use custom pipes 2 1/2" to 3" and run it through firewall?  seal the passanger compartment from carbon monozide real good  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  i am gonna try it one of these days.    ||||reg||11
Z||000005||stimpy||03-23-2001||10:37 PM||||Thanks for the props, y'all, but truth be told I was inspired by 1FST2M6 and Sluppy123. Nothing new under the sun.  As far as your idea for the rear trunk, Pat, I would think another concern would be the resonance from the engine that those ports would pick up. You wouldhave to wrap those tubes with a BUNCH of Dynamat to eliminate that noise. There are far easier ways to do the job. Check out my stuff next meeting and tell me if you still think its worth going through all that.<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||14
